    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d535">

                <pb facs="0545" n="511" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg511"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Mr.
                            Dupuy de Lôme.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-12-08"><hi rendition="#italic">December 8,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 321.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 6th instant in further reference to the matter of extending
                    to the unfortunate reconcentrados of Cuba charitable aid through voluntary <pb
                        facs="0546" n="512" xml:id="pg512"/> contributions of citizens of the United
                    States, and I have much pleasure in expressing the gratification which is here
                    felt on receiving your announcement that your Government has ordered that not
                    only articles of food shall be admitted free of duty, but also medicine,
                    clothing, or other articles of prime necessity which may be sent to Cuba in aid
                    of the reconcentrados or other needy persons in the island.</p>
                <p>The President, whose great interest in this matter has been thus shown and whose
                    humane motives are thus strongly appreciated by your Government, has the subject
                    under consideration.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Sherman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
